"contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: Hello Miranda. I've called you in to review our overall progress.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: I see. Where should we begin?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: Well, I haven't seen Peter in the past few days. How is he doing with the proposal?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: He's been quite focused since I dropped Greta's name the other day. He knows she shares his skill set. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: Peter must be feeling nervous.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: But returning to your point, his proposal is looking good.", "id": 1}, {"time": "29000", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: Glad to hear. On another note, how is Ferdinand? I haven't seen him since the meeting.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: Perhaps because he's been working so hard on punctuality. He's no longer in the hallways at irregular hours. Ferdinand is taking his new task seriously. I think he's thrilled to channel his PR skills into a South American context. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: You were right to recommend him. Good work. To change the subject, how's the new printer?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: Functions like a dream. What a relief!", "id": 2}, {"time": "58000", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: You can say that again! And now you, Miranda. I'm not concerned about your progress - I know that's all up to speed. How are you feeling about things?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: Honestly, until we have the proposal completed and hear back from Farmani I'm on pins and needles.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: I know exactly what you mean. Our success doesn't revolve around Holly's, but we're all anxious to know which direction we're headed in.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: That's it exactly. Well, we should know soon!", "id": 3}], "video_src": "engenn7le04ob03re2vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Preparing the Proposal"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Reviewing Progress"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le04ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Changing Topics in a Conversation"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When speaking a foreign language, especially English, it is important that you acquire a set of conversation strategies which will help you deal with the spontaneity of spoken English. A very important strategy you need to master is changing topics in a conversation. Here are a few expressions you can use to change the subject of a conversation."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Changing the subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Returning to the subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>By the way, ... </li><li>On another note, ... </li><li>Changing the subject,/ To change the subject, ... </li><li>On another note, ... </li></ul></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>Anyway, ...</li><li>As I was saying, ... </li><li>Returning to my point, ...</li></ul></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">To change the subject</span>, how's the new computer?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">On another note</span>, have you finished writing the report?"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Showing Understanding of Someone's Situation and Feelings "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When having a conversation in English, it is important to show that you are not only listening to someone explaining or telling you something, but also showing understanding of their situation and or feelings. Below you will find language that you can use to express understanding of someone's situation and/or feelings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">I see.</span> : You use this to show that you are paying attention and to show you understand what the person is saying<span class=\"italic\">.<ul><li>\u201cI'd like to talk to you about the new project.\u201d<br/>\u201c<span class=\"strong\">I see.</span>\u201d </li></ul></span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">I know what you mean.</span> : You use this to tell someone that you understand their situation well, perhaps because you have had a similar experience. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>\u201cI'm feeling nervous about this project.\u201d <br/>\u201c<span class=\"strong\">I know what you mean.</span>\u201d</li></ul></span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>Subject +  <span class=\"italic\">must be feeling</span> + adjective : You use this to tell someone that you understand how they or someone else feels. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>\u201c He seems quite focused today.\u201d <br/>\u201c<span class=\"strong\">He must be feeling nervous</span> after what you said.\u201d</li></ul></span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You can say that again</span> : You use this to show a strong agreement with what someone has said. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>\u201cThe new employee is really good.\u201d <br/>\u201c<span class=\"strong\">You can say that again!</span>\u201d </li></ul></span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Other ways of expressing understanding of someone's feelings and situation are:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">I know.</span> - meaning you understand someone and feel sympathy for them.</li><li><span class=\"italic\">I don't blame him/her.</span> - meaning you understand why someone did something or feels a particular way.</li><li><span class=\"italic\">Fair enough. </span>- meaning you understand and accept what someone says.</li></ul>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overall progress"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "how far something or someone has come along or progressed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's review our overall progress."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le04ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when discussing progress."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to put forward"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to propose for consideration"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hope the proposal has been put forward. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le04ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "focused "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "with your attention directed to what you want to do"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter seems very focused lately. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le04ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "irregular"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not happening at times that are at an equal distance from each other"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He's no longer in the hallways at irregular hours. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le04ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to drop a name"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to introduce someone into a conversation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He's been working hard since I dropped Greta's name the other day."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le04ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to channel"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to direct ideas towards a particular thing or purpose "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think he's thrilled to channel his PR skills into this project."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le04ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "up to speed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "performing at an expected rate or level"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I know we're all up to speed."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le04ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "skill set"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone's range of skills or abilities"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He knows that she shares his skill set. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le04ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of 7-10 conversation topics on a piece of paper."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Start a conversation with a partner using one of the topics. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you are ready, change the subject to one of the topics you have on your paper."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go back to a topic you were talking about when you can."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Keep going until you have run out of topics."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I think of conversation topics and start a conversation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I change the topic of a conversation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I go back to a previous topic in a conversation. "}]}]}